{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:02:13.613Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fec30a92d8d98f6016acb0a42978c8191a1137c36f1ebc2f9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6fb1f519d3854eddbd42f156010902f7","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n '^class CustomerData|^    [a-z_]+:' backend/customer_agent/ingest.py | head -28; head -24 backend/mappings/themes.yaml; sed -n '92,124p' backend/moderator/models.py; tail -1 output/council-rework/progress.jsonl; python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nx=json.load(open('output/council-rework/latest-export.json'))\\nfor e in x['events']:\\n if e['stage']=='moderation': print(e['statement'],e['data'])\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":1200}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","create_time":1791691330.6036282}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:02:13.714Z","type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1261a-2a92-7960-ad84-d63846639755","turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","session_id":"01a1261a-2a92-7960-ad84-d63846639755","root_turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","response_id":"resp_0fec30a92d8d98f6016acb0a322fbc8191a1e0ab4f729998ce","usage":{"input_tokens":187452,"cached_input_tokens":185216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":484,"reasoning_output_tokens":332,"total_tokens":187936},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5419227,"cached_input_tokens":5331712,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19066,"reasoning_output_tokens":6155,"total_tokens":5438293},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":179795765,"cached_input_tokens":175102464,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":824867,"reasoning_output_tokens":214511,"total_tokens":180620632}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:02:13.761Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a12920-2081-75e0-9aae-ceb746215410","call_id":"call_6fb1f519d3854eddbd42f156010902f7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f583c7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000009917,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1076,\"output\":\"29:class CustomerData:\\n30:    rows: pd.DataFrame\\n31:    records: pd.DataFrame\\n32:    studies: pd.DataFrame\\n33:    discovery: Discovery\\n34:    sources: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)\\n35:    warnings: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\\n93:    warnings: list[str] = []\\n129:    country_by_col: dict[int, str] = {}\\n173:    blocks: list[tuple[str, int, dict[str, dict[str, float]]]] = []\\n# Category / study-attribute label -> customer theme.\\n# Rules are checked in order; the first rule with a matching keyword, and no matching\\n# `exclude` keyword, wins. Keywords match whole words/phrases, case-insensitive; a\\n# trailing * matches any word ending (\\\"charg*\\\" = charge, charging, charger).\\n# A label that matches nothing becomes its own theme under its raw label: never\\n# dropped, never forced into a wrong group. Add keywords here for new datasets.\\n# `topic` is the nearest frontend Topic (src/lib/types) or null when none fits.\\n# `aliases` (optional) are everyday words used only to recognise the theme in free text,\\n# e.g. a council question (\\\"what about the screens?\\\"); they never classify source data.\\n\\nthemes:\\n  - theme: Charging & range\\n    topic: Charging\\n    aliases: [charg*, battery, batteries, ev, evs, electric, kwh, kw]  # free-text only (open discussion)\\n    keywords: [charg*, electric range, range, wallbox, high voltage battery, high-voltage,\\n               recuperation, regeneration, preconditioning, energy efficiency, fuel economy,\\n               electric mileage, mileage]\\n    exclude: [wireless, mobile device, phone*]\\n\\n  - theme: Infotainment & connectivity\\n    topic: Displays\\n    aliases: [screen*, touchscreen*, button*, idrive, menu*, ui, interface, connectivity, music, maps]  # free-text only (open discussion)\\n    keywords: [infotainment, information and entertainment, touch screen, screen interface,\\n               navigation, carplay, android auto, app, apps, operating concept,\\n    classification_rows: list[int] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n    classifications: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n    feedback_types: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n    topics: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n    quantitative: dict[str, Any] | None = None\\n    limitations: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n    excluded_reason: str | None = None\\n    # PDF tables stay unverified until an equipment extractor supplies exact row/column evidence.\\n    equipment_verified: bool = False\\n    derivative: str | None = None\\n    availability: Literal[\\\"standard\\\", \\\"optional\\\", \\\"unavailable\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"] = \\\"unknown\\\"\\n    dependencies: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n\\n\\nclass Catalog(Model):\\n    version: int = 1\\n    snapshot_hash: str\\n    created_at: str = Field(default_factory=now)\\n    sources: list[Source]\\n    evidence: list[Evidence]\\n    warnings: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n\\n\\nclass Rating(Model):\\n    value: float | None = Field(default=None, ge=0, le=5)\\n    evidence_ids: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n    rationale: str\\n\\n    @model_validator(mode=\\\"after\\\")\\n    def cited(self):\\n        if self.value is not None and not self.evidence_ids:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"A known rating requires evidence\\\")\\n        return self\\n{\\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-10-11T04:01:36.060175+00:00\\\", \\\"sequence\\\": 9, \\\"status\\\": \\\"running\\\", \\\"topic\\\": \\\"topic-controls\\\", \\\"stage\\\": \\\"challenges\\\", \\\"outcomes\\\": 0, \\\"active_seconds\\\": 129.512190627167, \\\"tokens\\\": 170649}\\nInvestigate whether the G60's infotainment system usability issues, as noted in customer feedback (G60_feedback:G60-0912 and G60_feedback:G60-3567), could be mitigated by adopting a rear-mounted control panel with physical buttons for essential functions, as suggested by the market perspective. {'round': 1, 'questions': {'customer': \\\"How would you address the usability issues in the G60's infotainment system, such as Android Auto integration and charging status visibility, while maintaining the high-quality ride and comfort praised in your feedback?\\\", 'market': \\\"What evidence would change the market's proposed test of integrating a rear-mounted control panel with physical buttons for essential functions in the G60?\\\", 'competitor': \\\"What specific competitor features or usability benchmarks would justify a conditional experiment to assess the G60's control accessibility during driving?\\\"}}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","create_time":1791691333.761626}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
