isuals and a measured final edit. Activate when the current request authorizes tha (file: r2/ai-host-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:faceless-video: Use only when the user asks to produce a finished multi-scene narrator-led video and explicitly requests a faceless channel, YouTube automation, narrated explainer/s (file: r2/faceless-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:higgsfield: Resolve and execute named Higgsfield presets and slash commands, or browse Viral and Marketing Studio preset galleries. Resolve a named preset before loading product (file: r2/higgsfield/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:motion-craft: Design concrete motion tracks for native Higgsedit compositions: frame choreography, timed text entrances, shared timelines and counters. Use for authoring how a nat (file: r2/motion-craft/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:narrator: Produce duration-constrained voice takes or a photo-based presenter overlay on an existing video. Use for explicit narrator invocation, numbered takes fitted to fixe (file: r2/narrator/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:subtitles: Use only when the current requested output is a video with speech captions permanently burned into its pixels, including restyling those captions or an explicit ca (file: r2/subtitles/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:thumbnail-generation: Create or revise finished YouTube/Instagram thumbnails and video cover images. Require a request to make or change the image; critique, readability analysis, title i (file: r2/thumbnail-generation/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:ugc-product-video: Produce a finished product-only UGC video with off-screen voiceover; a person may appear only as auxiliary hands, cropped body, or POV. Require UGC or casual creat (file: r2/ugc-product-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:ugc-try-on-video: Produce a finished UGC try-on video where one consenting adult or generated adult creator wears and poses with a garment, footwear item, bag, jewelry piece, or weara (file: r2/ugc-try-on-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:ugc-tutorial-video: Produce a UGC tutorial where one visible creator demonstrates realistic step-by-step use of a specific product and every step has a baked \"Step N — Heading\" label. (file: r2/ugc-tutorial-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:ugc-unboxing-video: Produce a creator-led UGC unboxing video: a visible creator opens a package and reacts to its reveal. Require both the creator-led format and an unboxing, haul or PR (file: r2/ugc-unboxing-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:ugc-website-video: Produce a finished creator-led UGC video about a website, web app, online service, store, or product page, using real captured screenshots while a talking-head cre (file: r2/ugc-website-video/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:video-editing: Edit footage and motion graphics with Higgsedit. Activate only for a requested edit or graphics deliverable: cuts, soundtrack changes, overlays and animated title  (file: r2/video-editing/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:website-builder: Build and publish a complete website, web app or browser game on Higgsfield, or edit/redeploy an existing Higgsfield-hosted site. Use when the requested deliverabl (file: r2/website-builder/SKILL.md)\n- app-6a3293e129088191abf0875820e839da:youtube-script: Write a complete YouTube script with a full spoken body in one of six genres: business/finance, tech review, commentary, documentary, true crime or explainer. Includ (file: r2/youtube-script/SKILL.md)\n- defense-factory:open-defense-factory: Open Codex Security Cloud for cloud security findings, scans, and continuous repository monitoring. (file: r3/defense-factory/0.1.1/skills/open-defense-factory/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Us (file: r10/documents/26.909.12148/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-code-connect: Creates and maintains Figma Code Connect template files that map Figma components to code snippets. Use when the user mentions Code Connect, Figma component mapping (file: r4/figma-code-connect/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-create-new-file: Always use this skill when the user wants to create a new Figma Design, FigJam, or Slides file. You MUST invoke this skill BEFORE every `create_new_file` tool call. (file: r4/figma-create-new-file/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-design-to-code: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — you MUST invoke this skill BEFORE calling the `get_design_context` Figma MCP tool. You MUST trigger this skill whenever the user wants to (file: r4/figma-design-to-code/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generate-design: Use this skill alongside figma-use when the task involves translating an application page, view, or multi-section layout into Figma. Triggers: 'write to Figma', 'crea (file: r4/figma-generate-design/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generate-diagram: MANDATORY prerequisite — load this skill BEFORE every `generate_diagram` tool call. NEVER call `generate_diagram` directly without loading this skill first. Trigger w (file: r4/figma-generate-diagram/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generate-library: Build or update a professional-grade design system in Figma from a codebase. Use when the user wants to create variables/tokens, build component libraries, create i (file: r4/figma-generate-library/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generative-plugins: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — load this skill before calling `create_generative_plugin` or `update_generative_plugin`. Use when the user asks to create, author, change (file: r4/figma-generative-plugins/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-implement-motion: Translates Figma motion and animations into production-ready application code. Use when implementing animation/motion from a Figma design — user mentions \"implement t (file: r4/figma-implement-motion/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-shaders: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — load this skill before calling `create_shader` or `update_shader`. Use when the user asks to create, author, change, fix, or iterate on (file: r4/figma-shaders/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-swiftui: SwiftUI ↔ Figma translation. Use whenever the user mentions Swift, SwiftUI, iOS, iPhone, or iPad — in EITHER direction — translating a Figma design into SwiftUI (de (file: r4/figma-swiftui/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — you MUST invoke this skill BEFORE every `use_figma` tool call. NEVER call `use_figma` directly without loading this skill first. Skippi (file: r4/figma-use/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use-figjam: This skill helps agents use Figma's use_figma MCP tool in the FigJam context. Can be used alongside figma-use which has foundational context for using the use_figma (file: r4/figma-use-figjam/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use-motion: Motion / animation context for the `use_figma` MCP tool — animating Figma nodes via manual keyframes, animation styles, easing, and timeline duration. Load alongs (file: r4/figma-use-motion/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use-slides: This skill helps agents use Figma's use_figma MCP tool in the Slides context. Can be used alongside figma-use which has foundational context for using the use_figma (file: r4/figma-use-slides/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-docs: Create and edit native Google Docs through connected tools. (file: r5/google-docs/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive: Use connected Google Drive as the single entrypoint for Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides work. Use when the user wants to find, fetch, organize, share, export, copy,  (file: r5/google-drive/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive-comments: Write, reply to, and resolve Google Drive comments on Docs, Sheets, Slides, and Drive files with evidence-backed location context. Use when the user asks to leave 