g, obser (file: r8/ai-gateway/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:ai-sdk: Vercel AI SDK expert guidance. Use when building AI-powered features — chat interfaces, text generation, structured output, tool calling, agents, MCP integration, st (file: r8/ai-sdk/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:auth: Authentication integration guidance — Clerk (native Vercel Marketplace), Better Auth, Descope, and Auth0 setup for Next.js applications, plus Sign in with Vercel, Ve (file: r8/auth/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:bootstrap: Project bootstrapping orchestrator for repos that depend on Vercel-linked resources (databases, auth, and managed integrations). Use when setting up or repairing a r (file: r8/bootstrap/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:build-agents: Default guidance for building AI agents. Use for generic requests to build, create, scaffold, design, architect, or implement an AI agent, agent app, tool-calling  (file: r8/build-agents/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:cdn-caching: Debug Vercel CDN caching — cache hit rate, stale content, revalidation behavior, ISR + PPR, per-request cache reasons (cacheReason) and PPR state (ppr_state), and  (file: r8/cdn-caching/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:chat-sdk: Vercel Chat SDK expert guidance. Use when building multi-platform chat bots — Slack, Telegram, Microsoft Teams, Discord, Google Chat, GitHub, Linear — with a singl (file: r8/chat-sdk/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:create-a-backend: Backend architecture guidance. Use when planning, building, or migrating an API or backend; choosing between Functions, Services, containers, Workflow, Queues, and (file: r8/create-a-backend/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:custom-metrics: Emit and query Vercel Custom Metrics. Use when instrumenting application or business measurements in Vercel Functions, using metric() from @vercel/functions, choos (file: r8/custom-metrics/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:deployments-cicd: Vercel deployment and CI/CD expert guidance. Use when deploying, promoting, rolling back, inspecting deployments, building with --prebuilt, or configuring CI workf (file: r8/deployments-cicd/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:domains: Search, register, connect, transfer, and renew domain names on Vercel using the CLI or Domains Registrar API. Use for domain availability and pricing, custom domains (file: r8/domains/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:env-vars: Vercel environment variable expert guidance. Use when working with .env files, vercel env commands, Secret or Config variable types, OIDC tokens, or managing envir (file: r8/env-vars/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:eve: eve framework guidance for durable AI agents and agent-powered applications. Use when creating, editing, or debugging an eve project, when the user explicitly asks f (file: r8/eve/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:flags-sdk: Set up and use feature flags and A/B tests with the Flags SDK (`flags` npm package) and Vercel Flags. Use when installing or configuring the SDK, adding a new or exi (file: r8/flags-sdk/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:is-agentic: Score how ready a website, domain, or public MCP endpoint is for AI agents using Is Agentic, and read or act on the resulting report. Use when asked to check a sit (file: r8/is-agentic/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:knowledge-update: Corrects outdated LLM knowledge about the Vercel platform and introduces new products. Injected at session start. (file: r8/knowledge-update/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:marketplace: Vercel Marketplace expert guidance — discovering, installing, and managing third-party integrations via the `vercel integration` CLI. Use when building any app tha (file: r8/marketplace/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:microfrontends: Guide for building, configuring, and deploying microfrontends on Vercel. Use this skill when the user mentions microfrontends, multi-zones, splitting an app across (file: r8/microfrontends/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:queues: Vercel Queues guidance — durable topics with at-least-once delivery, independent consumer groups, retries, delays, and idempotency keys via @vercel/queue (JS) or ver (file: r8/queues/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:react-best-practices: React best-practices reviewer for TSX files. Triggers after editing multiple TSX components to run a condensed quality checklist covering component structure, hook (file: r8/react-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:routing-middleware: Vercel Routing Middleware guidance — request interception before cache, rewrites, redirects, personalization. Works with any framework. Supports Edge, Node.js, and B (file: r8/routing-middleware/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:runtime-cache: Vercel Runtime Cache API guidance — ephemeral per-region key-value cache with tag-based invalidation. Shared across Functions, Routing Middleware, and Builds. Use  (file: r8/runtime-cache/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-agent: Vercel Agent guidance — dashboard and Slack chat, code review, production investigation, approved actions, and product installation. Use when configuring or working  (file: r8/vercel-agent/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-cli: Vercel CLI expert guidance. Use when deploying, managing environment variables, linking projects, viewing logs, querying metrics, managing domains, managing featur (file: r8/vercel-cli/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-connect: Vercel Connect expert guidance for securely obtaining scoped credentials for third-party services on behalf of apps or users. Use when wiring up provider API acces (file: r8/vercel-connect/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-firewall: Vercel Firewall expert guidance — automatic DDoS mitigation, the Vercel WAF (custom rules, IP blocking, managed rulesets, rate limiting), Attack Mode, system bypas (file: r8/vercel-firewall/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-functions: Vercel Functions expert guidance — Node.js/Bun/Python runtimes, Fluid Compute, long-duration (30 min) functions, large functions (5 GB bundles), Docker/OCI container (file: r8/vercel-functions/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-sandbox: Vercel Sandbox guidance — ephemeral Firecracker microVMs for running untrusted code safely. Supports AI agents, code generation, and experimentation. Use when execut (file: r8/vercel-sandbox/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-services: Configure and troubleshoot Vercel Services for multiple frontends and backends in one project. Use when composing a polyglot or multi-service application on one Verc (file: r8/vercel-services/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-storage: Vercel storage expert guidance — Blob, Global Config (formerly Edge Config), and Marketplace storage (Neon Postgres, Upstash Redis). Use when choosing, configuring,  (file: r8/vercel-storage/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:verification: Full-story verification — infers what the user is building, then verifies the complete flow end-to-end: browser → API → data → response. Triggers on dev server sta (file: r8/verification/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:workflow: Vercel Workflow SDK expert guidance. Use when building durable workflows, long-running tasks, API routes or agents that need pause/resume, retries, step-based exec (file: r8/workflow/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or (file: r1/visualize/1.0.45/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new Cha (file: r9/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real- (file: r9/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or estab (file: r9/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `workspace-write`: The sandbox permits reading files, and editing files in `cwd` and `writable_roots`. Editing files in other directories requires approval. Network access is restricted.\n\n`approvals_reviewer` is `auto_review`: Sandbox escalations with require_escalated will be reviewed for compliance with the policy.\nIf a rejection happens, you can continue with a safer alternative, or carry out checks to prove that the action is authorized or low risk before trying again. Complete unaffected work without asking for confirmation. Report anything that remains blocked, clarify why it was blocked by auto-review, inform the user of the risk and ask for approval.\n The writable roots are `/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var/folders/ys/r20k9fjs4dl_cltth8mkhlf80000gn/T`.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ctools\u003e\nDeferred tool namespaces:\n- mcp__codex_apps__apple_music: Searches the Apple Music catalog for specific artists, albums, songs, and playlists, and returns canonical catalog objects suitable for navigation or display. Also enriches model-generated song lists by batch-matching them to Ap...\n- mcp__codex_apps__canva: Create, review, edit designs\n- mcp__codex_apps__chatgpt_space: Read, search, create, and edit pages and spaces in ChatGPT Space, within your current account.\n- mcp__codex_apps__codex_document_control: Use Codex Document Control to find connected document sessions, inspect the tools supported by a selected session, and execute one supported tool against that session. Call `list_document_sessions` first to choose the intended c...\n- mcp__codex_apps__codex_security_cloud: Run security scans, investigate findings, and manage workflows for the current workspace.\n- mcp__codex_apps__figma: Create designs, ship to code\n- mcp__codex_apps__github: Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\n- mcp__codex_apps__gmail: Gmail tools for label counts, searching and reading emails/threads/attachments, reviewing drafts, and explicit mail changes like send, draft, forward, archive, Trash, and label actions.\n- mcp__codex_apps__google_drive: Search and work with files from Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides.\n- mcp__codex_apps__higgsfield: Every image and video model\n- mcp__codex_apps__hotline: Look up local helpline information for the user based on country inferred from the conversation. You must use this tool before providing a suicide or self-harm helpline; do not use web search or guess.\n- mcp__codex_apps__pets: Create and manage the user's animated companion pets inside ChatGPT Work mode. Use only for ChatGPT Pets, not real-world animal advice, generic pet images, or pets in other apps.\n- mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management: Manage plugins, settings, permissions, and connections. Prefer available built-in tools or connected plugins when they fit the task. Proactively search for plugins when an external app, account, or service would materially help,...\n- mcp__codex_apps__safety_settings: For ChatGPT Parental Controls (your child or teen's settings, features, Study Mode, quiet hours, family setup) and Trusted Contact (setup, status, privacy). Read account state first. Before updates, read the child's controls; pr...\n- mcp__codex_apps__search_service: Tool for accessing the internet.\n- mcp__codex_apps__shazam: Identify commercially recorded music playing in the user’s environment and then search, inspect, and contextualize that music using Apple Music catalog data (songs, albums, artists, playlists, charts). Also supports retrieving i...\n- mcp__codex_apps__sites: Use Sites to build or modify websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, portals, trackers, hubs, and internal tools. Use Sites skills for local implementation, source preparation, and artifact packaging. Use this...\n- mcp__codex_apps__supabase: Manage and query databases\n- mcp__codex_apps__ticketmaster: Search Ticketmaster For Events\n- mcp__codex_apps__tripadvisor: Enables searching for and viewing top-rated hotels on an interactive map, including filtering, sorting (e.g., by value, price, distance, popularity), and optionally obtaining live pricing, reviews, and amenities details for ind...\n- mcp__codex_apps__uber_eats: Use this to search for restaurants, cuisines, and specific dishes available for delivery within the user’s area on Uber Eats. Invoke it whenever the user expresses hunger or interest in food, takeout, restaurants, or delivery, ...\n- mcp__codex_apps__vercel: Provides access to documentation search for a specific hosting and deployment platform and tools to manage its projects and deployments, including listing projects, deployments, build logs, and creating temporary authenticated ...\n- mcp__node_repl: Use `js` for `node_repl` execution with persistent, redeclarable top-level bindings, `js_reset` to clear bindings, and `js_add_node_module_dir` to add package directories.\n\u003c/tools\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003crecommended_plugins\u003e\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Dropbox (app-69b31dc2110c8191b8b47dc98fe5a052@openai-curated-remote)\n- Atlassian Rovo (Legacy) (atlassian-rovo@openai-curated-remote)\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Codex Security (codex-security@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Calendar (google-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Linear (linear@openai-curated-remote)\n- Notion (notion@openai-curated-remote)\n- OpenAI Developers (openai-developers@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Calendar (outlook-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Email (outlook-email@openai-curated-remote)\n- SharePoint (sharepoint@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n- Teams (teams@openai-curated-remote)\n\u003c/recommended_plugins\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a1292f-d706-7360-b9d7-dfe70df98289","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","tools.deferred_namespaces","plugins.recommendations"],"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"`.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a1292f-d706-7360-b9d7-dff1e161f0ef","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a1292f-d706-7360-b9d7-e00a752b8a89","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-11\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eEurope/Berlin\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"managed\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"restricted\"\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:root\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:slash_tmp\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:tmpdir\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw/.git\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw/.agents\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw/.codex\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/shaur/ehlhackathonbmw/.aws\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003c/file_system\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n  \u003csubagents\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/customer_integration\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/judge_voice_integration\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/moderator_integration\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/bmw_assets\" /\u003e\n    \u003cagent name=\"/root/shader\" /\u003e\n  \u003c/subagents\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a1292f-d706-7360-b9d7-e01b8f58133d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"ok so basically now the plan okay I need to u know fix fully end to end the agent council it is already quite nice but there r some issues being the following yeah\n\n1\\) the conversation debate table part on the right yeah the conversation is sometimes a bit sus like not so clean and organised maybe if u must u can make sure the moderator is more active asks interesting relevant questions and the other agents ACTIVELY reply and must ACTIVELY argue with each others points as well as have a chance to say their own options clearly! okay? also why is the judge always just saying it recommends to deny or smth what defer it is yeah no that definitely needs fixing becuase at the end the judge should be able to produce a list of the new requirements for the future car basically and new features and stuff like that and send it clearly to the decisions and scenarios page btw for the PM to then manually accept or reject clean just green accept button and red reject button next to each okay and then also back to the agent council in the talk to jury part I currently need to scroll to see the icon the character I want it to be SUPER simplified I should see the character first and an audio button and stuff ja really clean\u0026#x20;\n\nalso now listen carefully for the proper fixed agent council implementation how it should work currentl there is this thing called full agenda and here: [http://127.0.0.1:5173/council?session=session-8fa8b13be42d4a0e\u0026advanced=1](http://127.0.0.1:5173/council?session=session-8fa8b13be42d4a0e\\\u0026advanced=1)\nThe moderator controls are completly messed up basically it should be super clean process when the PM at the beginning clicks start debate for example on the iX3 requirements in the future okay FIRST the moderator will give the list of the topics that should be discussed which the PM can check or not tick okay like range and efficiency, etc. etc. in the current frozen agenda and backlog section which is currently quite weird yeah after the PM then selects their selection from the apparently 59 candidates or smth? then the debate will start on the right side of the screen okay? but I recommend this moderator configuration I mentioned just now should open in a new window smaller window just like the voice agent part was before yeah but anyways after the PM selects that the debate starts with the moderator going through each selection step by step asking and prompting the agents to argue and say their POVs and deciding when each topic is done by the Jury making a final requirement if necessary for each selected topic okay? and note for each selected topic all the other agents should be able to not just give one like output but have a nice debate before the moderator stops that current sort of topic and the judge makes a requirement and the moderator moves on to the next selected topic got it? I have attached also some of these \"topics\" so called yeah.\n\nfirst fix this properly and make sure all the agents are PROPERLY having a debate and some are not saying weird answers okay? also u need to make sure that somehow none of the agents hallucinate and pull data either from the dataset which I am guessing how do we have it is it in the repo for it to access or? and furthermore if it uses data like for the competitor agent it must for example or even market trends it uses from reliable sources and cites quick yeah? also make the debate reallyyyy argumentative u know? and also later check the code and everything and fix the jury pls super important and tell me how exactly the jury decides whose opinions are correct yeah? \n","type":"input_text"},{"detail":"high","image_url":"data:image/png;base64,","type":"input_image"}],"id":"msg_01a12915-f240-7292-ab65-5f82864ba3be","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text","user.image"],"create_time":1791690666.56063,"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1261a-31a7-7643-b726-e44ac83c8595","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1261a-2c20-7071-9ea6-e30281de4f64"},"revision":"retained_01a1261a-31a7-7643-b726-e462c788697e"},"user_input_order":0},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a1261a-2c20-7071-9ea6-e30281de4f64","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12634-647e-7d53-aab4-351d5aea6fb0","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1261a-2c20-7071-9ea6-e30281de4f64"},"revision":"retained_01a12634-647e-7d53-aab4-353fc26c02ed"},"user_input_order":15},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a1261a-2c20-7071-9ea6-e30281de4f64","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-bundled","server_name":"cua_repl","tool_name":"js"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a12639-2f5f-7fb2-8415-f5a12a646a8f","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1261a-2c20-7071-9ea6-e30281de4f64"},"revision":"retained_01a12639-2f5f-7fb2-8415-f5cb566e3e21"},"user_input_order":18},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"first_turn_id":"01a1261a-2c20-7071-9ea6-e30281de4f64","plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@o