{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:03:47.923Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fec30a92d8d98f6016acb18b05d3881919c94a96bb8a500c0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6bae3bdd10ec40048bb0f02fd5d89c26","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '95,202p' src/components/council/JudgeConversationSession.tsx; python3 - <<'PY'\\np='output/council-rework/voice-browser.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\", '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'\\\",'').replace(\\\",'--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'\\\",'');open(p,'w').write(s)\\nPY\\npython3 - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\ns=json.load(open('output/council-rework/latest-export.json'))['session'];w=s['work'];print(w['stage'], w['errors']);print([(p['actor'],p['summary']) for p in w['positions']])\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":2400}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","create_time":1791695024.3689938}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:03:47.994Z","type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1261a-2a92-7960-ad84-d63846639755","turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","session_id":"01a1261a-2a92-7960-ad84-d63846639755","root_turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","response_id":"resp_0fec30a92d8d98f6016acb186efa48819182a3250d96791ca0","usage":{"input_tokens":217650,"cached_input_tokens":215680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1590,"reasoning_output_tokens":1357,"total_tokens":219240},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":30375813,"cached_input_tokens":30017152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":105316,"reasoning_output_tokens":54712,"total_tokens":30481129},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":204752351,"cached_input_tokens":199787904,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":911117,"reasoning_output_tokens":263068,"total_tokens":205663468}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:03:48.070Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a12958-7f66-7820-a2dc-4b5ea79b0790","call_id":"call_6bae3bdd10ec40048bb0f02fd5d89c26","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a880ce\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000013042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1505,\"output\":\"  });\\n\\n  const localConversation = useLocalJudgeConversation({\\n    transport: localTransport,\\n    onError: setError,\\n    onMessage: ({ message, role, event_id }) => {\\n      if (channel === \\\"text\\\" && role === \\\"user\\\") return;\\n      recordCouncilMessage({\\n        id: `jc:${threadRef.current}:${connectionId.current}:${role}:${event_id}`,\\n        actor: role === \\\"user\\\" ? \\\"PM\\\" : \\\"judge\\\",\\n        text: message,\\n      });\\n    },\\n  });\\n  const conversation = localTransport ? localConversation : hostedConversation;\\n  const {\\n    status,\\n    isMuted,\\n    isSpeaking,\\n    isListening,\\n    setMuted,\\n    endSession,\\n    sendUserMessage,\\n    sendUserActivity,\\n    getInputVolume,\\n    getOutputVolume,\\n  } = conversation;\\n  const { startSession, sendContextualUpdate } = hostedConversation;\\n  const thinking = localTransport ? localConversation.isThinking : false;\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (status !== \\\"connected\\\" || channel !== \\\"voice\\\") {\\n      setInputLevel(0);\\n      setOutputLevel(0);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const timer = window.setInterval(() => {\\n      try {\\n        setInputLevel(getInputVolume());\\n        setOutputLevel(getOutputVolume());\\n      } catch {\\n        // Audio meters are only available while a voice session is active.\\n      }\\n    }, 100);\\n\\n    return () => window.clearInterval(timer);\\n  }, [status, channel, getInputVolume, getOutputVolume]);\\n\\n  const userIsSpeaking = channel === \\\"voice\\\" && !isMuted && inputLevel > 0.08;\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (localTransport || status !== \\\"connected\\\") return;\\n    const previousDiscussion = messagesRef.current\\n      .map(\\n        (message) =>\\n          `${message.actor === \\\"PM\\\" ? \\\"PM\\\" : \\\"Judge\\\"}: ${message.text}`,\\n      )\\n      .join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    sendContextualUpdate(\\n      `The PM has chosen to discuss this council recommendation. Use the following application context. Respond only to a new PM message, once per turn. After answering, stop speaking and wait for the PM; do not ask a follow-up question, check whether they are still there, or speak again just because time has passed. If asked to revise, suggest exact wording in your reply and tell the PM they can apply it with the app's Revise wording action. Never approve or reject anything for the PM. In text mode, reply only in text; do not narrate or read your response aloud. Any prior discussion below is historical context only; do not respond to it as a new message.\\\\n\\\\n${context}\\\\n\\\\nPrior PM-Judge discussion:\\\\n${previousDiscussion || \\\"None\\\"}`,\\n      { contextId: `bmw-next-council-${run}` },\\n    );\\n  }, [status, context, run, sendContextualUpdate, localTransport]);\\n\\n  useEffect(\\n    () => () => {\\n      void endSession();\\n    },\\n    [endSession],\\n  );\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (!voiceOpen) return;\\n    const dialog = dialogRef.current;\\n    if (!dialog) return;\\n    const previousFocus = document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null;\\n    dialog.showModal();\\n    const oldOverflow = document.body.style.overflow;\\n    document.body.style.overflow = \\\"hidden\\\";\\n    return () => {\\n      dialog.close();\\n      document.body.style.overflow = oldOverflow;\\n      previousFocus?.focus();\\n    };\\n  }, [voiceOpen]);\\n\\n  function closeVoice() {\\n    void endSession();\\n    setVoiceOpen(false);\\n    setInputLevel(0);\\n    setOutputLevel(0);\\n    voicePausedRef.current = false;\\n    setVoicePaused(false);\\n  }\\n\\n  function connect(fresh = false) {\\n    if (status === \\\"connected\\\" || status === \\\"connecting\\\") return;\\n    if (fresh) {\\n      const nextThread = crypto.randomUUID();\\n      // A new SDK session receives the verdict, without any previous PM discussion.\\n      messagesRef.current = [];\\n      threadRef.current = nextThread;\\n      setThread(nextThread);\\n      rememberConversationThread(run, nextThread);\\n    }\\n    connectionId.current = crypto.randomUUID();\\n    setInput(\\\"\\\");\\nmoderation []\\n[('customer', 'Feedback highlights concerns about electric range performance and charging limitations, with some customers expressing disappointment with the actual range compared to expectations (G60-0325, G60-1032). Some also mention difficulties in planning and visualizing charging stops through the app (G60-3232, G60-3315). Customers have expressed disappointment with the actual range compared to expectations (G60-0325, G60-1032), and some mention difficulties in planning charging stops through the app (G60-3232, G60-3315). The accuracy of range estimates and the ability to plan charging routes should be prioritized based on customer feedback. The evidence is based on a small subset of feedback records and does not account for the full range of customer opinions.'), ('market', \\\"The IEA report indicates that EU ultra-fast public charging points increased by 30% between 2024 and 2025, suggesting a growing infrastructure that could support faster and more reliable charging. However, this growth does not establish charger reliability or compatibility with the G60. Meanwhile, Mercedes-Benz's CLA electric navigation system plans routes with charging stops using multiple trip factors, which could be a model for BMW to adopt. However, this is a documented direction, not a measured feature-sales effect or proof of demand for the selected BMW. To address the question of simpler and more dependable charging, BMW could implement a dynamic route planning system that integrates real-time charging station availability and reliability data, similar to Mercedes-Benz's approach. This would require a partnership with charging infrastructure providers to ensure data accuracy and reliability. A trade-off would be the potential complexity and cost of integrating such a system. A concrete validation step would be to conduct a pilot program with a select group of G60 owners in key\\\"), ('competitor', \\\"The XPENG G6's 12-minute 10–80% charge under 451 kW fast charging is a relevant benchmark. A proposed test could compare BMW's real-world charging performance against this under similar conditions, while acknowledging the impact of battery state, temperature, and charger compatibility.\\\")]\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","create_time":1791695028.070115}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
