{"timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:16:00.876Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a12963-adec-7512-8779-4ac206a2a8a7","call_id":"call_3b9c6e71df3f48838ce88230140ea2b6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fe4e7c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008084,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":656,\"output\":\"closure budget_exhausted valid False usage {'model_tokens': 347795.0, 'active_seconds': 680.8507621667814}\\n['What specific steps would BMW take to ensure real-time charging data integration in the G60 is compatible with the growing EU ultra-fast public charging network?', \\\"Does BMW's proposed integration of real-time public charging data into the infotainment system address the same customer concerns as the XPENG G6's fast-charging performance?\\\", 'competitor/rebuttal: AgentOutputError; no completed response', 'Missing rebuttal for topic-charging:customer:round1:challenge', 'Missing rebuttal for topic-charging:market:round1:challenge', 'Token reservation exhausted', \\\"discussion:topic-charging:competitor:round1:challenge: unsupported; The statement is not supported by any cited evidence. There is no evidence provided about the XPENG G6's charging performance or any comparison between BMW and XPENG. The claim is speculative and not grounded in the provided data.\\\", 'discussion:topic-charging:competitor:round2:challenge: unsupported; The statement is not supported by any cited evidence. The XPENG G6 benchmark is not mentioned in the provided evidence.']\\n[('customer', 'competitor', \\\"The customer feedback does not directly address fast-charging performance, so the XPENG G6 benchmark is a relevant comparison. A conditional test could assess BMW's real-world 10–80% charging time under similar conditions, while acknowledging battery state, temperature, and charger compatibility. This would validate the proposed feature without asserting BMW's absence of the capability.\\\"), ('market', 'competitor', \\\"The customer feedback does not directly address fast-charging performance, so the XPENG G6 benchmark is a relevant comparison. A conditional test could assess BMW's real-world 10–80% charging time under similar conditions, while acknowledging battery state, temperature, and charger compatibility. This would validate the proposed feature without asserting BMW's absence of the capability.\\\"), ('competitor', 'market', 'To directly address the challenge, BMW should refine its proposed integration of real-time public charging data by prioritizing user-centric features such as clear power-level visualization and route optimization based on real-time availability. This would directly respond to customer concerns about planning and visualizing charging stops (G60-3232, G60-3315). A trade-off is the increased data-processing complexity. A concrete validation step would be a pilot test in Germany with selected G60 units, measuring user satisfaction with route planning and power-level visibility.')]\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12915-f14a-7292-888b-5b2b4a685e60","create_time":1791695760.876504}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
